        "original_id": "c34d0977-4c35-5a1d-b214-f0461d1fb923",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: evil clown, traditional comic clown, horror elements, dark humor\n- Works: It\n- People: Stephen King\n- Characters: seven children, a fear-exploiting being\n\nFacts:\n- The evil clown is a subversion of the traditional comic clown character that makes the playful trope disturbing through horror elements and dark humor.\n- In 1986, Stephen King published It, a horror novel.\n- It was Stephen King's 22nd book and his 18th novel published under his own name.\n- The modern evil clown archetype was popularized by Stephen King's 1986 novel It.\n- It follows seven children who are terrorized by a being that exploits its victims' fears and phobias to disguise itself while hunting them.",
